# ── The library's CSS is hand-formatted, and that is load-bearing ──
#
# Tailwind emits declaration values with the source's own line structure, string
# quoting and number formatting, and tests/css/** asserts on the compiled text.
# Every setting in prettier.config.js changes that output:
#
#   printWidth: 100   rewraps long values, and one test checks that a defaulted
#                     colour space lands on its own line
#   singleQuote: true flips the WCAG rating strings ("AA" -> 'AA'), which
#                     if(style()) compares as token streams
#   (defaults)        drops the trailing zero from the 0.140 hueRotate matrix
#                     coefficient, and the space from calc(l * ...)
#
# Formatting these files takes the suite from 1659 passing to 912 failing. They
# were never prettier-clean; that is the intended state, not a backlog item.
packages/*/src/**/*.css
